<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="082" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rule selection by scope: direct core-record chain, eligibility and BU filter, per-type Replace / Additive precedence, unknown-BU finding</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172), wave W3-8</phase>
    <gate>080 and 081 done; Q1 (uac-r2) decides the BU column, interim B until then</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes which billing rules judge every invoice (eligibility, precedence, inheritance) and reads core records across the secure wall app-only; a widening or a silently dropped rule is a wrong judgement of a firm's invoice.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-relevant selection logic (fail-closed scope and chain) over ontology-owned and uac-r2-owned contracts, with review conditions from both.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>080, 081</deps>
    <tags>bff, rules, tenant-isolation, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement rule-set selection by scope (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 3.1-3.4 and 5.2): a CoreRecordChain reader (the invoice's core record plus its direct parents only), the pure RuleSetApplicability predicate, eligibility and the business-unit filter in BillingFactLoader, the per-type BillingRuleCatalogue.IsAdditive flag, and the lexicographic precedence for Replace types in InvoiceComplianceEvaluator, plus the interim unknown-business-unit finding.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the billing evaluator (tasks 070-073), Dataverse query batching and the uac-r2 filing maps.</role>

  <goal>Every MF / MNF control of design note section 8 rows Precedence, Combination, B2 / F1-b, Inheritance (direct only), BU filter and Fail-safe scope (rule sets) passes; a record-scoped set applies exactly to its record's invoices and its direct children's; nothing widens; the evaluator stays deterministic and inside NFR-01 on a 150-line invoice.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note sections 3 and 5.2; ontology-r1 conditions in section 12 (condition 4 and the non-blocking items). Decisions: D-39, D-116, D-136 / ontology D-171 (levels, BU filter, point 6 tie-break), D-137 / ontology D-172 (direct association only, no inheritance through an invoice or event; Q5 nearer wins; Q7 limits replace, checklists add; Q13 exact BU). Current code: BillingEvaluationRequest.CoreRecord (BillingFactLoader.cs:26-27); BillingRuleCandidate.Scope (:76); LoadAsync fault contract (:243-245); LoadRulesAsync (:280-379); evaluator D-39 block (InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs:264-299); system policy candidate (Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:1256); D-115 pattern (BillingEvaluationReasons in InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs:9-25 and :415; ReasonTemplate / ReasonHeadline in BillingRuleCatalogue.cs:234-236, :325, :357). uac-r2 maps: SecureRootInheritance.TypedFilingColumns (Services/Access/SecureRootInheritance.cs:401) and the project pair rule (:482).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/CoreRecordChain.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/RuleSetApplicability.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/BillingFactLoader.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/BillingRuleCatalogue.cs (IsAdditive; the unknown-BU reason template and headline)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs (:1256, Level = ClientDefault)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (CoreRecordChain registration; shared append point)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Signals/Billing/CoreRecordChainTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/Billing/RuleSetApplicabilityTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Signals/Billing/BillingFactLoaderTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/domain/Signals/Billing/InvoiceComplianceEvaluatorTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="080" status="pending">S1-S4 on dev</dependency>
      <dependency task="081" status="pending">RuleSetScope Record / FirmRecord values; validated record-scoped sets</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 (direct association only)">CoreRecordChain returns the invoice's core record at distance 0 and its DIRECT parents at distance 1, never more. Matter: itself only. Project: itself plus the matter or project its BFF-managed pair names. Work assignment: itself plus each record its typed sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingproject names. It never reads a parent's parent, never follows IntermediateFilingColumns (#1630: a work assignment under an invoice or event has a chain of itself only), and ignores a W pair no typed lookup repeats (#1616). One app-only row read, which also returns the business-unit column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 3.1, ontology-r1 condition 4">CoreRecordChain lives in Services/Signals/Billing/ and reuses SecureRootInheritance.TypedFilingColumns and the project-pair rule; it does not copy them and does not call FindFilingParentsAsync. ontology-r1 does the owner review; uac-r2 reviews the reuse of its maps.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 3.1, BillingFactLoader.cs:243-244">Fail closed: a chain row that cannot be read propagates as a Dataverse fault (the job retries). The invoice is never judged on a shortened chain.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-172 S2, design note 3.2">Eligibility: ClientDefault; Firm with sprk_firm = invoice firm; Record with exactly one core lookup whose record is on the chain; FirmRecord with both. A Record / FirmRecord set with no lookup (cleared by a delete) or two lookups is never eligible; a set whose firm was cleared never matches. Query filter plus a re-check of every row, as :304-315 does. One pure function RuleSetApplicability.AppliesTo(set, firmId, chain, homeBu) holds the predicate (083 reuses it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-171 points 3 and 6, D-172 Q13">BU filter is eligibility: a set with sprk_allbusinessunits No applies only when the home BU is on its list, exact match only (no parent / child match). One link-entity query for all sets, chunked at MaxInValues.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-172 Q7, design note 3.3">BillingRuleCatalogue.IsAdditive(RuleType): one exhaustive switch, throws on a non-billing type. Additive: ApprovedTimekeeper, NonBillableActivity, RequiredData, AiObservation, SubmissionIntegrity. Replace: ApprovedRate, TimeIncrement, DailyHoursCap, InvoiceAge, CoreRecordWindow, Duplicate. Split: ExpenseRule (owner, D-172 round 3). A test pins the full list (D-27: closed, reviewed as code); model the classification as a closed three-value enum (Replace / Additive / Split) rather than a bool, so the exhaustive switch keeps ExpenseRule visible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-172 round 3 (owner, #2129)">ExpenseRule is SPLIT, not a whole replace. Its per-category caps REPLACE: for each expense category, only the highest-ranked in-force version that sets a cap for that category is applied, and a category no specific version caps falls through to the less specific cap. Its non-reimbursable checklist ADDS: the union of `nonReimbursableCodes` across every in-force version at every level applies. Precedence and the ExpenseRule handler treat the two parts separately; do not split the rule type (no new sprk_ruletype option). No publish notice about dropped codes, because nothing is dropped. The B2 / F1-b rules still hold per part: a broken or downgraded specific version never removes a cap or a code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-171, D-172 Q5, design note 3.3">Replace types: rank = (Level, -Distance, BuSpecific) with Level ClientDefault 0, Firm 1, Record 2, FirmRecord 3 and Distance 0 or 1; only a gate-accepted, handler-accepted, not-downgraded version sets D(t); keep v iff accepted and rank(v) ≥ D(t). Additive types: keep every gate- and handler-accepted version (no displacement, the BU tie-break does not apply). B2 and F1-b behaviour unchanged. Ties apply. Order of output unchanged (policy code, then id).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 5.2 (Q1 open), ontology-r1 non-blocking item">Home BU: until uac-r2 answers Q1, a core record owned in the Secure Record business unit has an unknown home BU: only all-BU sets are eligible and the evaluator raises ONE invoice-level, flag-only finding with a new defined reason code (BillingEvaluationReasons, copying the D-115 currency pattern), never a free-text Signal. The Secure Record BU never matches a list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BillingRuleCandidate.Scope is replaced by Level, Distance and BuSpecific; InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs:1256 sets Level = ClientDefault for the system policy (D-125). No change to the Signals readers, SignalWriter or any sprk_policy column. Task 102 (if landed) and 101 reuse this loader; do not add a second scope filter anywhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: placement (billing evaluator, existing Services/Signals/Billing), publish-size delta, no package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md (sections 3, 5.2, 8, 12)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/tasks/072-invoice-compliance-evaluator.poml</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
