    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Loader rule-set read with re-check" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/BillingFactLoader.cs:280-379">Query filter, then every row re-checked; Dataverse faults propagate.</pattern>
      <pattern name="D-39 displacement" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Billing/InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs:264-299">Generalise in place from two ranks to the lexicographic rank.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Flag-only evaluation finding" location="InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs:9-25, :415; BillingRuleCatalogue.cs:234-236, :325, :357">The D-115 currency-skip finding: reason code, template, headline.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">git merge-base --is-ancestor 3c83d48cf HEAD. Dev data check (read-only): count sprk_workassignment rows with BOTH sprk_regardingmatter and sprk_regardingproject set, and for those, whether the matter equals the project's own matter. Record the counts.</step>
    <step order="1">CoreRecordChain and its tests (each table's chain; no second hop; intermediate ignored; untrusted pair ignored; unreadable row propagates).</step>
    <step order="2">RuleSetApplicability (pure) and its tests, one per eligibility row plus the cleared-lookup and two-lookup cases.</step>
    <step order="3">Loader: scope query, re-check through RuleSetApplicability, BU link query, Level / Distance / BuSpecific on the candidate; InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps :1256.</step>
    <step order="4">BillingRuleCatalogue.IsAdditive with the pinned-list test.</step>
    <step order="5">Evaluator precedence (Replace rank, Additive keep-all) and the unknown-BU finding.</step>
    <step order="6">Worked example of design note 3.4 as one seeded test (invoices on P, W1, W2); determinism test; NFR-01 timing on a 150-line invoice recorded.</step>
    <step order="7">Seeding proofs: (a) let CoreRecordChain add the parent's parent: the "M's set does not apply on W1" test must fail; (b) let a Record set with no lookup be eligible: the cleared-lookup test must fail. Restore and re-run.</step>
    <step order="8">dotnet build and dotnet test; publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="9">Reviews: ontology-r1 (owner review of CoreRecordChain and the evaluator change), uac-r2 (reuse of TypedFilingColumns and the pair rule). Record both.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="11">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/082-ruleset-scope-selection.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Q1 open: if uac-r2 has answered Q1 with a home-BU column, read it (sprk_homebusinessunit ?? owningbusinessunit, or as answered) instead of interim B; if the answer needs a column that does not exist yet on dev, keep interim B and report. Do not create the column (uac-r2 schema).</trigger>
    <trigger>If step 0 finds work assignments that carry both typed lookups where the matter is only the project's matter, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required: the data cannot express "under P only", so the owner's direct-only rule needs a decision (for example: when the W pair repeats one typed lookup, only that one is direct).</trigger>
    <trigger>If reusing TypedFilingColumns or the pair rule requires changing SecureRootInheritance (visibility or shape), STOP and ask uac-r2; do not copy the maps.</trigger>
    <trigger>If NFR-01 on a 150-line invoice is exceeded, STOP and report the measurement before optimising.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>BillingFactLoader (rule sets, policies, versions) and the D-39 block are extended in place. Core-record parents are known only to uac-r2's SecureRootInheritance (maps reused) and FindFilingParentsAsync (needs the provisioning graph, multi-hop and #1630-following, so it does not fit). No existing pure predicate decides rule-set applicability (GetFirmClauseAsync has its own two-scope switch at RuleSetService.cs:2052-2056).</existing>
    <extension>The loader and evaluator are extended. CoreRecordChain is new because the existing parent walk follows more than the direct parent and intermediates, which D-172 forbids for billing. RuleSetApplicability is new so the loader and the firm-clause check (083) cannot disagree.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A record-scoped rule set is never evaluated, so a matter's negotiated terms (D-171) never judge its invoices; without the per-type flag a matter's RequiredData rule would silently remove the client default's required fields (Q7).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">read-only step 0 count</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">CoreRecordChain.cs, RuleSetApplicability.cs, BillingFactLoader.cs, InvoiceComplianceEvaluator.cs, BillingRuleCatalogue.cs, InvoiceSubmissionAfterSteps.cs, FinanceModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">CoreRecordChainTests.cs, RuleSetApplicabilityTests.cs, BillingFactLoaderTests.cs, InvoiceComplianceEvaluatorTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/082-ruleset-scope-selection.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">CoreRecordChain: M → [M]; P under M → [P 0, M 1]; W typed under P → [W 0, P 1]; W typed under M → [W 0, M 1]; W under an invoice or event only → [W 0]; a W pair with no typed lookup adds nothing; an unreadable row throws (no partial chain).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">M's Record set applies to P's invoice and to W2's (W2 under M); P's set applies to W1's (W1 under P); M's set does NOT apply to W1's; P's set does NOT apply to M's own invoice; M2's set never applies under M1.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Record or FirmRecord set with no core lookup, or with two, is never eligible; a FirmRecord set of firm F2 never applies to F's invoice; a Firm set whose firm was cleared applies to nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Replace types: on P's invoice PRJ beats MAT and CD (ApprovedRate) and F+M beats CD (TimeIncrement); a FirmRecord set on the parent beats a Record set on the invoice's own record; uncovered types fall through; a refused MAT version leaves CD / FIRM in force; a downgraded MAT version runs as Flag beside CD.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Additive types: RequiredData of CD and MAT both apply; NonBillableActivity of CD and CD-Lit both apply; an Additive type is never displaced; IsAdditive returns the listed mode for each of the 12 billing types and throws on Threshold.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BU filter: a Litigation-listed set applies for a Litigation home BU and not for Corporate; a parent BU on the list does not match a child BU; at the same level and distance a BU-listed Replace set beats an all-BU one; with the home BU unknown (Secure Record BU) only all-BU sets apply and exactly one flag-only invoice-level finding with the new reason code is raised; the Secure Record BU never matches a list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The design note 3.4 worked example passes as one seeded test; output order is deterministic across runs; NFR-01 timing on a 150-line invoice recorded in notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proofs (a) and (b) recorded: each named test failed with the guard broken and passed when restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ontology-r1 and uac-r2 reviews recorded; publish-size delta recorded; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExpenseRule caps, must fire: on a project invoice with client-default cap $500 and project cap $1,000 for the same category, a $700 line is not flagged by the $500 cap and a $1,200 line is flagged by the $1,000 cap. Must not fire: the $500 default cap never fires alongside the project cap for that category.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExpenseRule caps fall through: a category the project version does not cap is still capped by the client-default version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExpenseRule checklist, must fire: client default lists E110 and the project version lists E101, so both E110 and E101 lines are found non-reimbursable on the project invoice. Must not fire: a code listed at neither level is not flagged.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>One adversarial-review pass by default; a second one because of the tenant-isolation tag (root CLAUDE.md section 8.5). Runs alone in P3-D (084 waits for 083, which edits RuleSetService.cs). The rate-card side of the chain is 085's; it reuses CoreRecordChain.</notes>

